From d87b74538c368cd7bebef64c5b81c5c377ae3f88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Azkali <a.ffcc7@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 18:39:38 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] src/adapters: add SystemSuspend HIDL system power control

Android 10 moved the suspend/wakelock loop out of libsuspend's
/sys/power/autosleep and into the android.system.suspend@1.0
SystemSuspend HAL, which owns /sys/power/wake_lock and runs the
autosuspend thread itself. Writing those nodes directly from repowerd
conflicts with the service on such devices.

Add an adapter that talks to ISystemSuspend over hwbinder and holds an
IWakeLock for the duration of any suspend disallowance, mirroring the
libsuspend allow/disallow bookkeeping. It is preferred over libsuspend
and falls back to it when hwbinder or the service is unavailable.
